many of the balls have grown faint and barely provide any illumination at
all.  The walls are lined with ragged tapestries whose scenes are all but
obliterated by a combination of burns, tears, and splashes of reddish-black
liquid.  The dull grey stone of the floor is pitted and marred by huge
scratches, though patches of polished stone gleam softly at random intervals.
