"A Walkway in the Ruined Shrine"
"This slender walkway runs down toward the raised dais at the northern end of
the chapel, skirting the stone benches that lie to the west.  Both the benches
and the walls have been ravaged, great chunks have been hewn roughly out of
the stone and splashes of a dried dark liquid are spattered everywhere.  The
remains of a thin red carpet cling to the middle of the walkway, reduced to a
shreds here and there.  The top six inches of the wall are lined with
beautifully carved runes and glyphs which are miraculously unmarred.  To the
north, an impenetrable blackness lies over the area.
"
"room to kneel and worship
