#60026
"A Ruined Shrine - A Hidden Tunnel"
"The soft dripping of water echoes through this area as small drops of water
collect, tremble, then fall down from the ceiling into the tiny pool that has
formed on the floor of the tunnel.  Torches are bracketed to the walls, though
they have long since burned away to merely charred sticks.  The roughly-carved
tunnel is narrow and cramped, and there seems to be no ventilation; the air is
stale and thick with age.  A small alcove is to the north, while the tunnel
