"A Ruined Shrine - A Small Alcove"
"This alcove is a mere depression in the rough stone, hollowed out haphazardly
at best.  A single bracket is affixed to the north wall; although no torch is
is held by the bracket, the area around it is covered in soot.  A faint
dripping sound can be heard to the south, the only ambient noise in the still,
lifeless air.  A crude wooden trap door with a thick iron ring lies in the
middle of the floor, held by clumsily made hinges.
